        "Jean-Loup Puget",
        "Lyman A. Page Jr."
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Precision maps of microwave background anisotropies made the early universe a quantitative experimental science and sharply constrained cosmological models.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Page led landmark mapping efforts, while Puget represents major contributions to complementary space observations; the field's progress spans several missions and teams.",
        "maturity": "The anisotropy pattern has been measured and cross-checked by successive experiments, with lasting scientific consequences.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit is distributed across COBE, WMAP, Planck, and many instrument and analysis teams.",
          "The candidate framing combines contributions from different missions and periods."
        ]
      }
    },
