      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Fast radio bursts revealed a new class of brief, extremely energetic cosmic events and have become a powerful probe of the universe.",
        "attribution": "Lorimer and collaborators identified the first burst in archival data; Bailes and McLaughlin were central to the discovery and its early interpretation.",
        "maturity": "The phenomenon is secure after discovery of many bursts by independent instruments, although the range of sources and emission mechanisms remains under study.",
